  "summary_en": "Converts a mono layer, VDB or attribute to RGB by passing its values through a colour ramp. It can apply input and output scaling and controls how values outside the input range are handled.",
  "inputs": [
    "source: the mono layer, VDB or attribute to convert",
    "ramp (optional): an RGB layer sampled along a horizontal line through the centre of the image; use it instead of the Ramp parameter"
  ],
  "key_parameters": [
    "Signature: the layer type the source accepts",
    "Compute Range: sets Input Min and Input Max to the source minimum and maximum",
    "Input Min / Input Max: source values mapped to the start and end of the ramp",
    "Output Min / Output Max: shift and scale the ramp's black and white points before it is applied",
    "Scale by Value: multiplies the ramp colour by the normalised input value, so output can keep brightening outside the ramped range",
    "Outside Range: Clamp at End pins out-of-range values to the ramp ends; Repeat cycles the ramp colours",
    "Ramp: the RGB ramp; the left side corresponds to Input Min and the right side to Input Max"
  ],
  "caveats": [
    "The page includes no explicit warning.",
    "The page suggests that if no ramping or clamping is needed, a mono layer can be wired directly into the destination node for an implicit RGB conversion."
